    ]
    statement """
        Promoting AQ Off causes two existing external-oracle tests to fail on HfMul/rate-target streams: jxl-oxide returns images differing from jpxl-decode by peak 255 and RMSE 115-126. The exact same streams are accepted by djxl, whose decoded output agrees with jpxl-decode at RMSE about 0.49. This localises the blocker to a jxl-oxide interoperability edge rather than a libjxl rejection, but the repository's intentional multi-oracle gate means the perceptual winner cannot be promoted by silently exempting jxl-oxide. Production defaults were reverted to Masking/quant_lf16/LF-fill-on; Off and fixed quant_lf remain opt-in research controls.
        """
