record jpegxl-rs.observation.phase5-aqoff-jxloxide-incompatibility-2026-08-11/3 : observation {
    title "jxl-oxide 0.12.6 narrows LfQuant at the signed-16-bit boundary"
    state verified
    scope [
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/rate.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/tests/vardct_oracle.rs"
    ]
    statement """
        The two failures originally attributed to HfMul are caused by optional LF fill producing otherwise-valid signed-32-bit G.2.2 LfQuant samples that jxl-oxide 0.12.6 narrows at the signed-16-bit boundary. A fixed-input black-box sweep agrees through quant_lf 78 (LF peak 32669, decoder peak 1) and fails at quant_lf 79 (LF peak 33088, decoder peak 255/RMSE 71.28); fixed HfMul values 1 through 65 remain decoder-consistent. Part 1 D.3 permits 32-bit Modular samples when modular_16bit_buffers is false, G.2.2 carries LfQuant through Modular, and djxl plus jpxl-decode agree, so this is an external-decoder defect rather than a JPXL wire error. The fixed-quantizer API retains the standard's full signed-32-bit range. Target-rate LF fill now declines only candidates whose planned LfQuant exceeds signed 16-bit, preserving compatibility without weakening the oracle gate. All 10 VarDCT oracle tests pass afterward.
        """
    observed_at git:25213f6821b695e5b60a8d34c785a09aed9ee327
    method command
    watches [
        "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/rate.rs",
        "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/tests/vardct_oracle.rs",
        "JPXL/crates/jpxl-decode/src/vardct/**"
    ]
    derived_from [ @jpegxl-rs.observation.phase5-quality-policy-screen-2026-08-11/3 ]
    supersedes [ @jpegxl-rs.observation.phase5-aqoff-jxloxide-incompatibility-2026-08-11/2 ]
    verified_by [
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase5-candidate-djxl-self-agree-2026-08-11,
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase5f-lfquant-boundary-2026-08-11,
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase5f-oracle-gate-2026-08-11
    ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.observation.phase5-quality-policy-screen-2026-08-11/1 : observation {
    title "AQ Off plus quant_lf 8 is the first corpus-gated VarDCT perceptual policy"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/field.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs"
    ]
    statement """
        A matched-target, symmetric-djxl screen on three unique test-set photographs establishes two production policy changes. First, the single-pass activity field is disabled by default: AQ Off lowers Butteraugli versus Masking by 10.2%, 31.6%, and 31.8% on the three scenes, while Uniform remains far behind Off on the 4.3 MP screen. Second, the rate-target policy uses quant_lf 8 with secondary LF fill disabled: versus 16, it improves both Butteraugli and SSIMULACRA2 on all three scenes, with Butteraugli changes of -7.3%, -3.8%, and -0.2%. Together, the two changes reduce Butteraugli versus the old policy by 16.8% on the dense-detail 1 bpp scene and about 34% on the flat/edge 2 bpp scene. This is real progress but does not establish the 20%-of-cjxl goal: the corrected equal-rate small-photo anchor remains much farther away. Negative screens prune Gaborish, forced DCT8 cover, and EPF iteration signalling without filter planning. Raw commands, hashes, tables, and default-control fingerprints are in .agent/scratch/phase5-aq-broaden-QyUSZ8/summary.md. Measurements were made on a dirty worktree based at 25213f6 and remain diagnostic until committed and re-run.
        """
    observed_at git:25213f6821b695e5b60a8d34c785a09aed9ee327
    method command
    watches [
        "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/field.rs",
        "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs",
        "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs"
    ]
    derived_from [ @jpegxl-rs.observation.aq-field-is-a-net-perceptual-loss-2026-08-10 ]
    verified_by [
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase5a-aq-policy-gate-2026-08-11,
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase5b-gaborish-negative-2026-08-11,
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase5c-lf-hf-balance-2026-08-11,
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase5d-fixed-cover-negative-2026-08-11,
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase5e-epf-signalling-noop-2026-08-11
    ]
}

