record jpegxl-rs.observation.phase5-quality-policy-screen-2026-08-11/5 : observation {
    title "AQ Off plus quant_lf 8 is the target-rate default but remains outside the cjxl goal"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/field.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/tests/rate_loop.rs",
        path "test-set/**"
    ]
    statement """
        The Phase 5G broader gate measured the historical Masking/quant_lf16/LF-fill policy against AQ Off/quant_lf8/no-LF-fill on six distinct photographs at one and two bpp, decoding every stream through the same pinned djxl. The candidate reduces Butteraugli distance by 7.6% to 34.2% in all twelve cells and improves RMSE in all twelve. SSIMULACRA2 improves in ten cells but regresses by 0.3665 and 4.3685 on two 1-bpp scenes. The target-rate constructor and CLI therefore promote the candidate under the revised bounded Contract B; fixed-quantizer defaults remain unchanged. Request tests pass 4/4, rate-loop integration passes 11/11 with one ignored diagnostic, the independent-decoder suite passes 10/10, and the untouched CLI output is byte-identical to the measured candidate. Equal-rate cjxl effort-7 anchors show JPXL still has 26.6% to 85.9% higher Butteraugli distance, so this is a meaningful default improvement rather than completion of the within-20% goal. The mid2/2 cjxl anchor belongs to the initial 841754-byte candidate, not the later 795208-byte matched-policy rerun. Negative screens continue to prune Gaborish signalling alone, forced DCT8 cover, and EPF iteration signalling without filter planning. Raw commands and tables are in .agent/scratch/phase5-aq-broaden-QyUSZ8/summary.md, .agent/scratch/phase5f-lfquant-compat-2026-08-11.md, and .agent/scratch/phase5g-corpus-summary-2026-08-11.md.
        """
    observed_at git:25213f6821b695e5b60a8d34c785a09aed9ee327
    method command
    watches [
        "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/field.rs",
        "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs",
        "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
