record jpegxl-rs.observation.phase5-quality-policy-screen-2026-08-11/7 : observation {
    title "One active EPF step remains best globally; structural candidates are content-dependent"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/field.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/lib.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/tests/rate_loop.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/tests/vardct_oracle.rs",
        path "test-set/**"
    ]
    statement """
        Phase 5G promoted AQ Off, quant_lf 8, and no LF-fill after improving Butteraugli in all twelve six-scene cells by 7.6% to 34.2%. Phase 5H showed lower global quant_lf is content-dependent. Phase 5I promoted one active EPF step with uniform Sharpness 7 after it improved Butteraugli, RMSE, and Butteraugli pnorm3 in all twelve cells; the target-rate default remains byte-identical to that screened candidate. Phase 5J tested a structurally different two-pass HF reconstruction-error AQ field. At exact byte caps it regressed both 1-bpp direction cells; its lone 6.2% Butteraugli win lost 0.7443 SSIMULACRA2, so the temporary mode was removed. Phase 5K tested deeper active EPF. Three steps improved Butteraugli in nine of twelve cells but regressed three by up to 7.2% and lost up to 6.03 SSIMULACRA2; uniform Sharpness 3 and 5 did not remove the inconsistency, so those temporary controls were removed and one step remains production. Against the existing equal-rate cjxl effort-7 anchors, the production policy is still within 20% Butteraugli on only two of twelve cells and remains 23.8% to 78.1% worse on the other ten. The durable direction is now content/spatially adaptive restoration or LF/HF planning, not another frame-wide constant. Raw tables are in .agent/scratch/phase5g-corpus-summary-2026-08-11.md, .agent/scratch/phase5h-quantlf-tail-2026-08-11.md, .agent/scratch/phase5i-active-epf-2026-08-11.md, .agent/scratch/phase5j-two-pass-error-2026-08-11.md, and .agent/scratch/phase5k-active-epf-depth-2026-08-11.md.
